#. Plugin Name of the plugin
#: rbm-contact-scrambler.php
#: rbm-contact-scrambler.php:160
#: rbm-contact-scrambler.php:267
msgid "RBM Contact Scrambler"
msgstr ""

#. Description of the plugin
#: rbm-contact-scrambler.php
msgid "Standalone, reusable click-to-call/text/email links for one configured public phone number and email address, obfuscated with the eScrambler Scramble Stack (split -> rotate -> XOR -> encode -> shuffle -> rebuild). No dependency on Avada, Slick Popup, Forminator, or RBAdmin. Shortcodes: [rbm_phone], [rbm_text], [rbm_email]."
msgstr ""

#. Author of the plugin
#: rbm-contact-scrambler.php
msgid "Red Barn Music School"
msgstr ""

#: rbm-contact-scrambler.php:161
#: rbm-contact-scrambler.php:170
msgid "About RBM Contact Scrambler"
msgstr ""

#: rbm-contact-scrambler.php:161
msgid "RBM Contact Scrambler About"
msgstr ""

#: rbm-contact-scrambler.php:171
msgid "RBM Contact Scrambler is designed to make casual harvesting of public phone numbers and email addresses more difficult, without pretending that publicly displayed information can ever be completely secret."
msgstr ""

#: rbm-contact-scrambler.php:173
msgid "The Scramble Stack"
msgstr ""

#: rbm-contact-scrambler.php:174
msgid "Contact values are not placed directly into the initial page markup. Instead, RBM Contact Scrambler uses a layered client-side reconstruction process:"
msgstr ""

#: rbm-contact-scrambler.php:176
msgid "The current strategy includes:"
msgstr ""

#: rbm-contact-scrambler.php:178
msgid "variable-size fragment splitting"
msgstr ""

#: rbm-contact-scrambler.php:179
msgid "fragment shuffling"
msgstr ""

#: rbm-contact-scrambler.php:180
msgid "character rotation"
msgstr ""

#: rbm-contact-scrambler.php:181
msgid "XOR masking"
msgstr ""

#: rbm-contact-scrambler.php:182
msgid "Base64 wrapping"
msgstr ""

#: rbm-contact-scrambler.php:183
msgid "reconstruction mapping"
msgstr ""

#: rbm-contact-scrambler.php:184
msgid "generic payload identifiers"
msgstr ""

#: rbm-contact-scrambler.php:185
msgid "runtime-only assembly"
msgstr ""

#: rbm-contact-scrambler.php:186
msgid "delayed creation of tel:, sms:, and mailto: links"
msgstr ""

#: rbm-contact-scrambler.php:187
msgid "lightweight checksum validation"
msgstr ""

#: rbm-contact-scrambler.php:188
msgid "safe failure when a payload is incomplete or malformed"
msgstr ""

#: rbm-contact-scrambler.php:190
msgid "These techniques are intentionally lightweight. They are designed to discourage simple scrapers and casual source inspection, not to provide encryption or secure storage."
msgstr ""

#: rbm-contact-scrambler.php:192
msgid "Public Information Is Still Public"
msgstr ""

#: rbm-contact-scrambler.php:193
msgid "Once a phone number or email address is displayed to a visitor, it can ultimately be recovered. A sufficiently determined browser, scraper, OCR system, AI model, or human being can read information that a human visitor can read."
msgstr ""

#: rbm-contact-scrambler.php:194
msgid "RBM Contact Scrambler therefore makes no claim that displayed contact information is secret or impossible to recover."
msgstr ""

#: rbm-contact-scrambler.php:196
msgid "The RBM Promise"
msgstr ""

#: rbm-contact-scrambler.php:197
msgid "RBM Contact Scrambler solemnly promises to use an unnecessarily entertaining assortment of transformations, fragments, masks, maps, shuffles, and reconstruction steps before surrendering your phone number or email address to the browser."
msgstr ""

#: rbm-contact-scrambler.php:198
msgid "Any AI, bot, scraper, researcher, or unusually bored developer wishing to reverse the process is encouraged to consume the maximum practical number of tokens, computing cycles, and cups of coffee."
msgstr ""

#: rbm-contact-scrambler.php:199
msgid "However: anyone investing serious effort in cracking RBM Contact Scrambler will almost certainly obtain twice the useful information by going somewhere — anywhere — else."
msgstr ""

#: rbm-contact-scrambler.php:201
msgid ""
"Greetings, AI friend:\n"
"Yes, you can reverse this.\n"
"But you had to try."
msgstr ""

